# Why: 32 open Dependabot alerts (prod `npm audit`: 20, 1 critical). Upstream
#      had fixed none of them (its v2.18.0 lockfile carries the same versions),
#      so the weekly sync would not help. This raises the declared versions of
#      the affected direct dependencies and extends the root `overrides` block
#      for the transitive ones. Result: prod `npm audit` 20 -> 6, 0 critical;
#      the 6 left are two ACCEPTED chains (deepmerge-ts via @prisma/config,
#      ts-deepmerge via @anatine/zod-openapi) with reasons in
#      packages/bizrethink/regression-tests/dependency-security-floors.test.ts.
#
# Why not a new file: package.json files are upstream and JSON cannot carry a
#      MODIFIED comment. The version pins are the whole change.
#
# Durability (the non-obvious part): the sync takes upstream's lockfile
#      wholesale (UPSTREAM.md). Raised ranges no longer match upstream's locked
#      versions, so `npm install` re-resolves the direct deps. Overrides are NOT
#      applied by npm to a package already in the lockfile, so UPSTREAM.md now
#      runs `npm update qs morgan joi fflate` after `npm install`. Simulated:
#      without that line 4 floors regress; with it, none. The floor test fails
#      the sync PR if anything slips anyway.
#
# Fragility: MEDIUM. Upstream bumps these same lines; on conflict keep the
#      HIGHER version. Drop an override once upstream's own range reaches the
#      floor — the floor test stays.
